      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is some of this stuff in `before_test()` and some in `test_init()`? I guess `test_init()` runs one time and `before_test()` runs before each of your two tests?\n\nSeems like all of this stuff should be in `before_test()`, then. As documented in `unit_tests.md`: \"Unit tests should be independent from each other as much as possible\", so really your 2nd unit test shouldn\u0027t really be depending on the state of the system at the end of your 1st unit test, right?",
