      "writtenOn": "2023-03-17T18:52:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see your point, test should be independent from each other.\nhaving said that, I want to limit setting the GPIOs outside the test code as much as possible: \n\nWithout\n\u0027\u0027\u0027\ngpio_set_level(GPIO_LID_OPEN, 0);\ngpio_set_level(GPIO_TABLET_MODE_L, 1);\n```\nthe emulator set both GPIO to low, so the GMR sensors would indicate the device lid angle is both 0 and 360 degree. Setting one GPIO up is required.\n\nBetween tests, that condition should not happen. If it does, I want to be able to detect it. I also wanted to detect unwanted state changes - especially in the next CL where sensors and GPIO are interacting together.\n\nAnother alternative is to have only one single big test.",
