      "writtenOn": "2023-03-20T08:18:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e What is the point of trying to detect things that happen between tests?\n\nSet the GMR in lid close state in before_test() as you initially recommended.\n\n\u003e Also: what of my worry that I\u0027ve detected an actual bug while poking around. Specifically if you\u0027re in tablet mode and then (lid_open\u003d1, tablet_mode_l\u003d0) and then you quickly tablet_mode_l\u003d1 lid_open\u003d0 at the same time (before tablet_mode_l has a chance to debounce) then you\u0027ll miss a transition. That seemed like a valid issue.\n\nGood catch. It should not happen in the wild, since the lid has to physically mode from closed to flip. Note that we need 3 valid lid angle calculation in the same angle domain (so at least 3x100ms) to change to call tablet_set_mode(). \nHowever, by defining a priority in debouncing, it could be mitigated.\nAdded a test to confirm.",
